# Docs at the end of a task

Once, when the task is done, update the docs this change made stale. Not after every file.

## Write

- The colocated `README.md` next to the code: what the behavior is now, and why it left an existing plan if it did. If files were added, renamed, or removed in that folder, update that README's file list. Edit the stale sentences. Do not rewrite a whole section for a one-line change.
- `docs/SPEC_MAPPING.md` only when a spec item moved between missing / partial / implemented.
- `docs/DESIGN_STYLE.md` only when the visual standard itself changed.
- A parent README (`components/README.md`, `app/README.md`) or the root `README.md` only when a user-facing overview sentence is now false.

## Skip

`docs/tree.md`, `docs/tree.txt`, screenshot recapture, and unrelated docs. File-header comments stay in the source. Skip `docs/BRAIN2_FEATURE_IDEAS.md` unless the work was about that idea bank.

The tree, the gallery, and a repo-wide sync are a separate pass: `.cursor/rules/doc-sync.mdc`. Run that when asked to update the tree, sync docs, refresh the gallery, or prepare a push.

```text
❌ BAD: after each new file, regenerate tree.txt and recapture screenshots
✅ GOOD: finish the feature, then fix the stale sentences in components/Lists/README.md
❌ BAD: ship a new default and leave the plan describing the old one
✅ GOOD: in that same end-of-task pass, say what was decided and why
```
